{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363653-sanguine-saber-chosen-of-grandmother-bright-wip","id":1363653,"title":"Sanguine Saber, Chosen of Grandmother Bright (WIP)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-27T10:30:19-08:00","id":1363653,"title":"Sanguine Saber, Chosen of Grandmother Bright (WIP)","content":"While looking for any 3rd Edition info for Chiaroscuro this weekend, I was inspired by <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/exalted/comments/2k05xl/oh_chiaroscuro_how_i_love_you/\" target=\"_blank\">this reddit thread </a>to make an Exigent for my upcoming game. With my players largely being associated with the criminal elements in the city, I thought she'd make a good antagonist for them. She still needs some final touches I think, so any suggestions would be appreciated.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Sanguine Saber, Avenger of Grandmother Bright</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When Grandmother Bright shed her mantle as the goddess of vengeance and betrayal, she selected a champion to carry on her work. The Exalt carries her Exigence imbedded within the eponymous blade that once formed part of the goddess\u2019 panoply. For generations, this Exigence has been passed down from one bloody Avenger to the next, each taking the sobriquet of the Sanguine Saber to continue the grim work of their predecessor. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The current Sanguine Saber dwells in the Plaza in Chiaroscuro, having sought the mentorship of Grandmother Bright years ago. Officially she serves the Celestial Bureaucracy and upholds its laws among the gods. When not pursuing rogue gods across Creation alongside Sidereals, she spends her time stalking the Chiaroscuro\u2019s lawless slums and Undercity. She is regarded as one of the most ruthless bounty hunters in the city. While she\u2019d never never turn down a hefty bag of silver for her work, she can be found working </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>pro bono</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> for an impoverished citizen abandoned by the law as often as she can working for a wealthy noble or Guild factor. Adopting another\u2019s vendetta drives her more than the promise of coin.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Essence:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 3, </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Willpower:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 6, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Join Battle:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">8 dice (+3 for 3m or +5-7 for 5-7m)</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Personal Motes: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">13, </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Peripheral Motes:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">35</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Health Levels:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> -0/-1x2/-2x2/-4/Incap</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Attributes</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength 4, Dexterity 5, Stamina 3, Charisma 3, Manipulation 3, Appearance 3, Perception 4, Intelligence 2, Wits 5</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Abilities</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Awareness 3, Athletics 3, Dodge 3, Integrity 5 (Against Mercy), Investigation 3, Larceny 2, Linguistics 1, Lore 1, Melee 5 (The Sanguine Saber), Presence 4 (Threats), Resistance 2, Stealth 2</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Combat</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attack (The Sanguine Saber): 14 dice (+5 for 5m or +7-11 for 7-11m; damage 16, minimum 5)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Combat Movement: 8 dice</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Evasion: 3 (+1 for 2m or +2-3 for 4-6m), Parry: 7 (+2 for 4m or +3-4 for 6-8m)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Soak/Hardness: 8 / 0 (5 for 3m) (Chiaroscuro glass lamellar)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><i>Powers:</i></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Excellencies:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The bearer of the Sanguine Saber may add up (Ability) dice to an action with their Excellency. If they are attack in support of a negative Tie, they may increase this to (Ability + Intimacy): +2 / +3 / +4 for Minor, Major, and Defining Intimacies, respectively.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Sanguine Saber:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Exalt carries the name of the blade that holds her Exigence, the Sanguine Saber. The two cannot long be separated. She adds (Essence +1) to the difficulty to disarm gambits against her while she wields the saber. She may reflexively spend 1 mote to summon the blade to her hand on her turn, causing it to pass through Elsewhere if necessary. Finally, if she is slain in battle, the blade cries out for vengeance. The next wielder of the Sanguine Saber gains a Defining Intimacy against the character or characters who slew the previous wielder, which cannot be eroded while the perpetrator lives. The Sanguine Saber\u2019s successor knows only as much about her killers as she did in life. The successor may be required to due further investigation to identify them in detail.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><i>Offensive Charms</i></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Title</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">3m; Reflexive; One Scene; None</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): Sizing up her foe before a fight, the Sanguine Saber readies herself against his treachery. After a successful read intentions action during which she discovered a character\u2019s hostile intent, she may activate this Charm. For the rest of the scene, she adds her threshold successes on the read intentions roll to her Initiative to determine if she acts before the designated character.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Title</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2m, 1i; Supplemental; Instant; Perilous, Withering-Only</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): The Sanguine Saber brings every advantage to bear against a hated foe. She increases the minimum damage of her </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">withering</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> attack by 1. If she possesses a negative Tie toward her target, she also increases by minimum damage by her Intimacy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Anger\u2019s Cruel Daughter</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (4m; Supplemental; Instant; Decisive-Only): The Sanguine Saber is unwavering in her pursuit of vengeance. She adds (Integrity) dice to the raw damage of a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">attack. If attacking an enemy toward whom she has a negative Tie, she may also spend 1 Willpower to convert up to (Intimacy) dice into successes.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Title</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(2m; Supplemental; Instant; Uniform): The Sanguine Saber revels in her foe\u2019s suffering. She gains bonus dice on the attack equal to her target\u2019s wound penalty, plus 2 if she has a negative Tie toward the target.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Title</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(4m; Supplemental; Instant; Uniform): The Sanguine Saber\u2019s ire surges in the presence of a hated foe. She doubles up to (Integrity) 9s on her attack roll. If she has a negative Tie against the target, she doubles up to (Integrity) 8s as well. If she has a Major or Defining Tie against the target, she also doubles up to (Integrity) 7s.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Backstabbing Bliss Technique</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">6m, 1wp; Simple; Until next turn; Dual</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): Ever-vengeful, the Sanguince Saber is always prepared to lash out as those who strike against her. After an opponent has rolled an attack against her but before damage is rolled, the Sanguine Saber makes a counterattack against them. She may perform either a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">withering</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> or a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">attack. If she possesses a negative Tie toward her opponent and either crashes them or inflicts 3+ levels of </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> damage, she adds (Intimacy) to her Initiative. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><i>Defensive Charms</i></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Title</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">6m; Reflexive; Indefinite; Decisive-Only</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): Against a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> attack, the Sanguine Saber gains (Integrity) -2 health levels. If she possesses a negative Tie toward her attacker, she also gains extra -4 health levels equal to the Intimacy. If she already has this Charm active when she is attacked by another enemy toward whom she possesses a stronger negative Tie, she gains additional -4 health levels to make up the difference. For the duration of this Charm, her wound penalty is applied as a non-Charm bonus to her Defense rather than as a penalty.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Title</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">3m; Reflexive; Instant; Decisively-Only</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): The Sanguine Saber steels herself against the vicious blows of her enemies. She gains Hardness (Integrity/2, rounding up) against a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> attack. If she possesses a negative Tie against her attack, she adds it to her Hardness from any source.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><i>Social Charms</i></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Title</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2m; Supplemental; Instant; None</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): Expecting betrayal at every turn, the Sanguine Sabre re-rolls 1s on read intentions rolls until they fail to appear. If she possesses a Tie toward the character, she also doubles 9s.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Your Fight Is Mine</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2m; Reflexive; Instant; None</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): If another character successfully performs an inspire action against the Sanguine Saber, informing her of some wrong they have suffered, she may immediately gain an appropriate negative Minor Tie of vengeance directed against the party believed to have done the misdeed instead of (or in addition to) whatever emotion the influencer had hope to impart. If she already had a suitable Tie, she regains 1 Willpower instead. Limit once per scene.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blood-Clad Horror</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2m; Supplemental; Instant; None</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): The Sanguine Saber may apply her Appearance to threats and attempts to inspire fear as if she had the Hideous Merit, subtracting a minimum of 1 from the target\u2019s Resolve. If she has a negative Tie toward the threatened individual, she adds the Intimacy to her Appearance.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Fang-Hiding Smile</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">4m; Reflexive; Indefinite; None</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): The Sanguine Saber\u2019s Guile is increased by her negative Intimacies in the same manner as her Resolve if another character attempts to discern them or her motives regarding the subject of her ire by reading her intentions.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Vengeance\u2019s Relentless Hand</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u2014; Permanent; Permanent; None</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): If a plea for mercy or forgiveness would be opposed by the Sanguine Saber\u2019s negative Intimacies, the bonus to her Resolve is doubled. If it is also opposed by her Defining Intimacy, it becomes an unacceptable influence. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blood Demands Blood</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (3</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">m, 1wp; Simple; One Story; None</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): The path of vengeance is not walked by the Sanguine Saber alone. This Charm is a special persuade action to convince another character to pursue vengeance against some actual or perceived offense against them, adding the Sanguine Saber\u2019s (Essence) in bonus dice. If successful, the persuaded individual gains non-Charm bonus dice on any action that enhances his quest for vengeance, based on how difficult recovering from the offense would be as a task: +1 for inconvenient, +2 for serious, +3 for life-changing.</span></span><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Pursuit Charms</i></span></span></i><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Title</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">3m, 2i; Reflexive; Instant; Perilous</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): The Sanguine Saber never abandons the pursuit of her foe. She may Rush reflexively on her turn. If she has a negative Tie toward the target of her rush and succeeds on the roll, she gains Initiative equal to the Intimacy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Title</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u2014 [2m]; Permanent; Permanent; None</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): Once per day, if the Sanguine Saber comes within Short Range of any location where a character toward whom she possesses a negative Tie has been in the last day, she becomes aware of this at no cost. She may then commit 2 motes to grant any Awareness, Investigation, or Survival roll made during that Scene to follow-up +1 non-Charm bonus success.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2118,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","user":"Reminiscent Oasis","date":". 01-28-2020, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T12:39:13-08:00","id":1363667,"title":"","content":"That's a lot of Charms, are you sure you'll be able to remember them and apply all of them correctly?<br /> <br /> (And, in addition to being a lot of them, more than a couple are also hideously unfair.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T13:07:06-08:00","id":1363669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363653-sanguine-saber-chosen-of-grandmother-bright-wip?p=1363667#post1363667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a lot of Charms, are you sure you'll be able to remember them and apply all of them correctly?<br /> <br /> (And, in addition to being a lot of them, more than a couple are also hideously unfair.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you elaborate on &quot;hideously unfair&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T13:39:57-08:00","id":1363673,"title":"","content":"Great character write-up, It's so fleshed out I think it could actually make a fun Exigent PC.<br /> <br /> On the &quot;The Sanguine Saber&quot; Power : It's basically a superior version of Solars' Call the Blade, is this intended? Also increasing the difficulty of disarms seems rather superfluous when the weapon can be Reflexively teleported back to its wielder at will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T21:51:44-08:00","id":1363736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363653-sanguine-saber-chosen-of-grandmother-bright-wip?p=1363673#post1363673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great character write-up, It's so fleshed out I think it could actually make a fun Exigent PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I made her more detailed than a typical QC because I'm hoping she'll be a recurring character. Hopefully the PCs don't decide to kill her off the first chance they get. Of course, she's considerably more combat-focused than any of them, so she should have a decent chance at surviving if a fight breaks out. If they do manage to defeat her, that's what the Defining Intimacy to avenge the predecessor is for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the &quot;The Sanguine Saber&quot; Power : It's basically a superior version of Solars' Call the Blade, is this intended? Also increasing the difficulty of disarms seems rather superfluous when the weapon can be Reflexively teleported back to its wielder at will. </div> </div> </div>In her case, the blade and Exalt are one in a way that the Solar duelist and his are not. So I could justify giving her a better version of Call the Blade than a Solar as far as her one signature weapon is concerned. This is likely filling the niche of an anima power rather than a Charm proper. Haven't considered what her anima power(s) would be yet otherwise, if she has any. <br /> <br /> As for the disarm aspect, you're right, it would be a bit redundant so I tweaked the Call the Blade portion of that power so she can only recall the blade reflexively on her turn, allowing a brief window where she can be disarmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2118,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","user":"Reminiscent Oasis","date":". 01-28-2020, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T03:55:53-08:00","id":1363766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363653-sanguine-saber-chosen-of-grandmother-bright-wip?p=1363669#post1363669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you elaborate on &quot;hideously unfair&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Her fifth attack Charm is nuts. Since she has Integrity 5, she'll basically always double all 9s on the attack roll, <i>plus</i> she gets to double all 8s on a ridiculously easily triggered condition, <i>plus </i>she gets to double even 7s on a not particularly difficult condition. On a Uniform Charm. For 4 motes.<br /> <br /> For comparison, Bleeding Crescent Strike doubles 9s for 5m, and also 8s if you're attacking a battle group (which basically guarantees you won't actually need the double 8s, except for withering threshold successes). Perfect Blazing Blow costs a willpower and doubles (essence) total successes, with 9s first and 8s if your target is crashed (ie. you're winning). Double 7s on attack rolls are practically unheard of.<br /> <br /> Against an opponent she has even a minor Intimacy for, she can bring 14 + 7 + 2 = 23 dice to bear, with double 8s on the roll, for an average of <b>16 </b>successes. A fully minmaxed Dawn with a medium weapon can go up to Parry 7 base + 5 excellency + 1 stunt + 1 willpower = 14. The greatest warrior known to the world <i>might </i>parry her average attack roll result by going all-out, <i>if</i> said warrior has Essence 3 and the Sanguine Saber rolls at least three 1s or 2s. And she gets to do this as long as she mildly dislikes someone. On withering <i>and </i>decisive attacks.<br /> <br /> <br /> Her first defensive Charm is similarly overtuned. For 6m, she gets up to 9 additional Health Levels, <i>and </i>she gets to convert her wound penalties to Defense bonuses. As a Reflexive. This is basically a flat-out better version of Iron Skin Concentration + Battle Fury Focus (total cost: 13 motes and an action). Hell, this might be even better than Iron Skin Concentration + Battle Fury Focus + Bloodthirsty Sword-Dancer Spirit (total cost: 23 motes, 1 willpower, two actions), since the Defense bonus is non-Charm. And the weird thing is that you <i>didn't</i> have to do this - it would be trivial for you to just give her two Ox-Bodies of your choice and let the Charm give her (Intimacy) additional Health Levels. It would even be a buff!<br /> <br /> <br /> Some of her social Charms are also overtuned, but frankly, I can't muster the will to care about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T05:10:48-08:00","id":1363775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363653-sanguine-saber-chosen-of-grandmother-bright-wip?p=1363766#post1363766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Her fifth attack Charm is nuts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see your point on that one. I had Stalking Cat Movement Meditation in mind for comparison, but didn't remember all the details right on that one. I'll probably add a 1wp cost to it and change it to (Integrity/2, rounding up) instead of full Integrity to bring it more in line with that Charm. I'll consider de-Uniforming it as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Her first defensive Charm is similarly overtuned. </div> </div> </div>I considered mounting a brief defense of this considering that -0hls are worth more than the -2hls and the situation -4hls, but you raise a fair point that an Ox-Body streamlines this whole thing quite a bit. The Defense bonus I could probably strip out as a separate charm, which would fill a niche I had in mind but never got around to for her. I'll admit, when I wrote up this draft, I had a tendency to lump a bunch of effects together as one &quot;Charm&quot; for simplicity's sake, but still ended up writing a lot more Charms for her than I originally expected to.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the input. If the spirit takes you later and you feel like critiquing the Social Charms too eventually, I'd be happy to hear it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T06:13:42-08:00","id":1363782,"title":"","content":"What's making some of these charms seem rather overtuned to me is that as it stands she could have some really broad &quot;guilty by asosciation&quot; intimacies and have no difficulty at all harnessing her full power against people who don't even know they're in her way. So it might be a good idea that some of the charms which key off of negative intimacies to require the Sanguine Saber hold an intimacy of hated towards the target specifically rather than have misgivings towards people like them.<br /> <br /> I don't have an issue with the idea of her overpowering a Dawn Caste who she's personally sworn vengeance against, but less so one whose stumbled into her path by accident while she was hunting a dangerous criminal, therefore they must be also be a criminal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T10:44:05-08:00","id":1363813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363653-sanguine-saber-chosen-of-grandmother-bright-wip?p=1363782#post1363782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's making some of these charms seem rather overtuned to me is that as it stands she could have some really broad &quot;guilty by asosciation&quot; intimacies and have no difficulty at all harnessing her full power against people who don't even know they're in her way. So it might be a good idea that some of the charms which key off of negative intimacies to require the Sanguine Saber hold an intimacy of hated towards the target specifically rather than have misgivings towards people like them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I intended her to work anyhow, with the exception of her Excellency since that one only requires that she be upholding a negative tie rather than targeting the subject of the negative Tie. If she has a vendetta against the Guild, she could use her Excellency to undermine it in anyway, but couldn't use her Offensive Charms to beat up some random Guild merchant she's never met before. Maybe at higher Essence levels she could start dabbling in that sort of broad applicability, but that sort of thing would likely <i>just</i> be kicking in at Essence 3, perhaps letting her seek vengeance against collective involving a small handful of people. A Sworn Kinship of Dragonblooded, for example, but not their assorted retainers and soldiers. If this were the case, she'd only be able to focus on one such group at a time, likely locked in via a RIghteous Lion-like Charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T11:09:58-08:00","id":1363823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363653-sanguine-saber-chosen-of-grandmother-bright-wip#post1363653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><i>Social Charms</i></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Title</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2m; Supplemental; Instant; None</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): Expecting betrayal at every turn, the Sanguine Sabre re-rolls 1s on read intentions rolls until they fail to appear. If she possesses a Tie toward the character, she also doubles 9s.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blood-Clad Horror</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2m; Supplemental; Instant; None</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): The Sanguine Saber may apply her Appearance to threats and attempts to inspire fear as if she had the Hideous Merit, subtracting a minimum of 1 from the target\u2019s Resolve. If she has a negative Tie toward the threatened individual, she adds the Intimacy to her Appearance.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The first one probably should be 3m if comparing to solar and lunar charms that do something similar.<br /> <br /> For the second one I don't really know what you mean with it 'subtracting a minimum of 1 from the target's Resolve', unlike 2e appearance doesn't subtract anything from the targets Resolve but adds non-charm dice equal to appearance - resolve. Or do you mean you subtract 1 from the targets resolve before comparing it to appearance?<br /> <br /> It also doesn't say the intimacy can increase her Appearance over 5, if it can it should probably be 3m in line with lunars Myriad Graces Appeal which does about the same thing (Blood-Clad Horror is a bit more narrow but it also has the double effect of also giving you temporary hideous).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363653-sanguine-saber-chosen-of-grandmother-bright-wip#post1363653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blood Demands Blood</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (3</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">m, 1wp; Simple; One Story; None</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): The path of vengeance is not walked by the Sanguine Saber alone. This Charm is a special persuade action to convince another character to pursue vengeance against some actual or perceived offense against them, adding the Sanguine Saber\u2019s (Essence) in bonus dice. If successful, the persuaded individual gains non-Charm bonus dice on any action that enhances his quest for vengeance, based on how difficult recovering from the offense would be as a task: +1 for inconvenient, +2 for serious, +3 for life-changing.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I first read this as being to one action but it seems to be to every action toward the goal untill vengeance is achieved? If so that's nuts. I'd spam it on all my circle-mates to swear vengeance on any big-bad we come up against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 01-28-2020, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T11:19:18-08:00","id":1363827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363653-sanguine-saber-chosen-of-grandmother-bright-wip?p=1363813#post1363813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is how I intended her to work anyhow, with the exception of her Excellency since that one only requires that she be upholding a negative tie rather than targeting the subject of the negative Tie.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually I think your concept has a bit more untapped potential - the Sanguine Saber isn't an Exigent of Strong Negative Opinions, she's an Exigent of Vengeance. The nice thing about the (Intensity) framework is that you can basically apply it to <i>anything</i>. The Core only cares about Intimacies, Derangements and disease, but there's nothing stopping you from declaring Aggrievements on a Minor, Major and Defining scale, using the guidelines on persuasion to determine what's worth what (so inflicting a loss equal to what someone would be willing to lose for the sake of a Defining Intimacy is a Defining Aggrievement, et cetera).<br /> <br /> I think this would make your concept come across more strongly than it does in its current incarnation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T11:42:53-08:00","id":1363831,"title":"","content":"Thanks, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2579\" data-vbnamecard=\"2579\">limaxophobiac</a>. Good points all around. With Blood-Clad Horror in particular I was getting 2e interference with that one.<br /> <br /> As for Blood Demands Blood, it is intended to enhance the character for the rest of the story (or as long as the Sanguine Saber feels like keeping the 3m committed). It's intended to fill in the training niche. But double checking against Charms like Tale-Spinning Mastery, it may be too broadly applicable. On one hand, it's temporary and requires a commitment, unlike TSM, but on the other hand, it provides 3 dice to a wide range of actions rather than a total of 3 dice on up to 3 Abilities. Perhaps it should grant a temporary specialization toward pursuing vengeance in 1-3 Abilities of the target's choice, with the number of Abilities determined by the severity of the offense. Alternatively, I could make it &quot;Once per story.&quot; I'd say reset if the subject of the vendetta is defeated, but that's likely the end of the story anyhow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T11:50:53-08:00","id":1363832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363653-sanguine-saber-chosen-of-grandmother-bright-wip?p=1363827#post1363827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I think your concept has a bit more untapped potential - the Sanguine Saber isn't an Exigent of Strong Negative Opinions, she's an Exigent of Vengeance. The nice thing about the (Intensity) framework is that you can basically apply it to <i>anything</i>. The Core only cares about Intimacies, Derangements and disease, but there's nothing stopping you from declaring Aggrievements on a Minor, Major and Defining scale, using the guidelines on persuasion to determine what's worth what (so inflicting a loss equal to what someone would be willing to lose for the sake of a Defining Intimacy is a Defining Aggrievement, et cetera).<br /> <br /> I think this would make your concept come across more strongly than it does in its current incarnation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I likely will pursue something like that in the next draft of the character. I've been a little hesitant to embrace something like that, since originally I didn't want to introduce a new mechanic like that. But it's increasingly seeming like something akin to a Minor, Major, and Defining Vendettas will help focus her Charms and prevent things like &quot;mild annoyance&quot; from triggering them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T22:00:36-08:00","id":1363913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363653-sanguine-saber-chosen-of-grandmother-bright-wip#post1363653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><i>Offensive Charms</i></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Title</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">3m; Reflexive; One Scene; None</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): Sizing up her foe before a fight, the Sanguine Saber readies herself against his treachery. After a successful read intentions action during which she discovered a character\u2019s hostile intent, she may activate this Charm. For the rest of the scene, she adds her threshold successes on the read intentions roll to her Initiative to determine if she acts before the designated character.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>A Study in Retribution Observation?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363653-sanguine-saber-chosen-of-grandmother-bright-wip#post1363653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Title</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2m, 1i; Supplemental; Instant; Perilous, Withering-Only</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): The Sanguine Saber brings every advantage to bear against a hated foe. She increases the minimum damage of her </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">withering</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> attack by 1. If she possesses a negative Tie toward her target, she also increases by minimum damage by her Intimacy.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Spite-Empowered Hammering?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363653-sanguine-saber-chosen-of-grandmother-bright-wip#post1363653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Title</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(2m; Supplemental; Instant; Uniform): The Sanguine Saber revels in her foe\u2019s suffering. She gains bonus dice on the attack equal to her target\u2019s wound penalty, plus 2 if she has a negative Tie toward the target.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Revelry in Another's Misfortune Practice?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363653-sanguine-saber-chosen-of-grandmother-bright-wip#post1363653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Title</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(4m; Supplemental; Instant; Uniform): The Sanguine Saber\u2019s ire surges in the presence of a hated foe. She doubles up to (Integrity) 9s on her attack roll. If she has a negative Tie against the target, she doubles up to (Integrity) 8s as well. If she has a Major or Defining Tie against the target, she also doubles up to (Integrity) 7s.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Quickening to Final Settlement Rush?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363653-sanguine-saber-chosen-of-grandmother-bright-wip#post1363653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><i>Defensive Charms</i></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Title</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">6m; Reflexive; Indefinite; Decisive-Only</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): Against a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> attack, the Sanguine Saber gains (Integrity) -2 health levels. If she possesses a negative Tie toward her attacker, she also gains extra -4 health levels equal to the Intimacy. If she already has this Charm active when she is attacked by another enemy toward whom she possesses a stronger negative Tie, she gains additional -4 health levels to make up the difference. For the duration of this Charm, her wound penalty is applied as a non-Charm bonus to her Defense rather than as a penalty.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Unbroken Obstinatcy Stance?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363653-sanguine-saber-chosen-of-grandmother-bright-wip#post1363653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Title</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">3m; Reflexive; Instant; Decisively-Only</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): The Sanguine Saber steels herself against the vicious blows of her enemies. She gains Hardness (Integrity/2, rounding up) against a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> attack. If she possesses a negative Tie against her attack, she adds it to her Hardness from any source.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Righteous Durability Spirit?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363653-sanguine-saber-chosen-of-grandmother-bright-wip#post1363653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><i>Social Charms</i></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Title</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2m; Supplemental; Instant; None</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): Expecting betrayal at every turn, the Sanguine Sabre re-rolls 1s on read intentions rolls until they fail to appear. If she possesses a Tie toward the character, she also doubles 9s.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Appreciation of Expected Duplicity Method?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363653-sanguine-saber-chosen-of-grandmother-bright-wip#post1363653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Pursuit Charms</i></span></span></i><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Title</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">3m, 2i; Reflexive; Instant; Perilous</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): The Sanguine Saber never abandons the pursuit of her foe. She may Rush reflexively on her turn. If she has a negative Tie toward the target of her rush and succeeds on the roll, she gains Initiative equal to the Intimacy.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Lightning-Hot Revenge Serving?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363653-sanguine-saber-chosen-of-grandmother-bright-wip#post1363653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Title</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u2014 [2m]; Permanent; Permanent; None</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">): Once per day, if the Sanguine Saber comes within Short Range of any location where a character toward whom she possesses a negative Tie has been in the last day, she becomes aware of this at no cost. She may then commit 2 motes to grant any Awareness, Investigation, or Survival roll made during that Scene to follow-up +1 non-Charm bonus success.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Signs of Nemesis Recognition?<br /> <br /> <br /> Just some suggestions. Hope they are of use or at least give you ideas of your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-29-2020, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T07:32:46-08:00","id":1363963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363653-sanguine-saber-chosen-of-grandmother-bright-wip?p=1363813#post1363813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is how I intended her to work anyhow, with the exception of her Excellency since that one only requires that she be upholding a negative tie rather than targeting the subject of the negative Tie. If she has a vendetta against the Guild, she could use her Excellency to undermine it in anyway, but couldn't use her Offensive Charms to beat up some random Guild merchant she's never met before. Maybe at higher Essence levels she could start dabbling in that sort of broad applicability, but that sort of thing would likely <i>just</i> be kicking in at Essence 3, perhaps letting her seek vengeance against collective involving a small handful of people. A Sworn Kinship of Dragonblooded, for example, but not their assorted retainers and soldiers. If this were the case, she'd only be able to focus on one such group at a time, likely locked in via a RIghteous Lion-like Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. It's probably fine for your intended purposes since you're unlikely to give them major/defining intimacies for the sake of an exploit, but when it comes to evaluating the value of charms there's always been people eager to trade their character's sanity for power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}